<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nasry Asfura</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1958">1958</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nasry Asfura (born 1958) is a Honduran businessman and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-party-south-africa">National Party</a> politician who served as mayor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tegucigalpa">Tegucigalpa</a> from 2014 to 2022. He lost the 2021 presidential election to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiomara-castro">Xiomara Castro</a> but narrowly won the disputed election of November 2025 after a slow and contested count, and he took office as president in January 2026.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nasry-asfura.jpg" alt="Nasry Asfura" width="320" height="436" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DHSgov · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Honduras_President_Nasry_Asfura.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
